      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Logical Validation Pipeline \n",
      "fontSize": 28,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Logical Validation Pipeline \n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "-bp2PsW36FJYS9PQU8Kin",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 5174.304997755704,
      "y": 18640.606404410428,
      "width": 684.123779296875,
      "height": 560,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b6L",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 2006063354,
      "version": 1106,
      "versionNonce": 1097948026,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1785321809328,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Current:- We consider that whatever data has \nreached in the offline tables is absolutely \ncorrect. But the problem is that on the serving \nside is that making sense, means are we providing \nenough data to prove the scores?\n\nSolution:- A 2 Phase Logical Validation pipeline\nwhich can checks if the data on the serving side \nis making sense or not?\n\nPhase/ Layer 1:- Checks the current setup if the\ndata which is currently in serving layer along with \nnew data which needs to be put in serving layer\n\nPhase/Layer 2:- Checks if the data is correctly \nentered in the serving layer and is readable",
      "fontSize": 28,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Current:- We consider that whatever data has \nreached in the offline tables is absolutely \ncorrect. But the problem is that on the serving \nside is that making sense, means are we providing \nenough data to prove the scores?\n\nSolution:- A 2 Phase Logical Validation pipeline\nwhich can checks if the data on the serving side \nis making sense or not?\n\nPhase/ Layer 1:- Checks the current setup if the\ndata which is currently in serving layer along with \nnew data which needs to be put in serving layer\n\nPhase/Layer 2:- Checks if the data is correctly \nentered in the serving layer and is readable",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "5SsvBThCTKfNtEoMxjnnR",
      "type": "rectangle",
      "x": 4370.991125174267,
