      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1785319677595,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Inter Dag Pipeline\n",
      "fontSize": 28,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Inter Dag Pipeline\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "4Zkqhg1w876xx4I5hhoIJ",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 4400.74349082543,
      "y": 18690.644473914654,
      "width": 674.5758666992188,
      "height": 560,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b6O",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1249429114,
      "version": 855,
      "versionNonce": 1025802662,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1785320499505,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Current:-  Each dag has individual runs,  which\nmeans that the upper layer dag wont get \naffected by the lower layer dag runs. \n\nProblem:- Suppose in case of any node or stream \nfailure the data in raw table wont come, which \nwill Cause the issue that the above features \nwill get calculated wrongly, which will ultimately \nimpact the scores\n\nSolution:- An Inter dag pipeline. It will check if\nthe data for the previous days are present\nor not with other checks. If and only if the \nchecks get passed then only the higher level\ndags will be triggered. And then a report will \nget generated ",
      "fontSize": 28,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Current:-  Each dag has individual runs,  which\nmeans that the upper layer dag wont get \naffected by the lower layer dag runs. \n\nProblem:- Suppose in case of any node or stream \nfailure the data in raw table wont come, which \nwill Cause the issue that the above features \nwill get calculated wrongly, which will ultimately \nimpact the scores\n\nSolution:- An Inter dag pipeline. It will check if\nthe data for the previous days are present\nor not with other checks. If and only if the \nchecks get passed then only the higher level\ndags will be triggered. And then a report will \nget generated ",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
